// Syncthing ignore patterns for the mtga-mcp database.
//
// mtga-mcp is set up to sync a single SQLite DB (mtga.db) across machines by pointing
// MTGA_MCP_DB_PATH at a folder inside your synced tree (e.g. ~/Documents/mtga-mcp/mtga.db).
// Append these lines to the .stignore at the ROOT of that Syncthing folder (adjust the
// "mtga-mcp/" prefix to match the DB's location within the folder).
//
// They exclude SQLite's transient sidecar files, which must NOT be synced — syncing them
// mid-write can corrupt the database. mtga.db itself is safe to sync because MTGA (and thus
// capture) only runs on one machine at a time and our writes are short rollback-journal
// transactions, leaving a clean single file at rest.

mtga-mcp/*-journal
mtga-mcp/*-wal
mtga-mcp/*-shm
